  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Parc naturel départemental de la Grande Corniche covers 712 hectares between La Trinité, Villefranche-sur-Mer, Èze and La Turbie, from Mont Leuze to Mont Bataille. It's a vast area of scrubland and pine forest overlooking the French Riviera, with several spectacular viewpoints over the bay of Villefranche, Cap Ferrat and, on a clear day, as far as the Principality of Monaco.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The park's official regulation, published by the Département (Randoxygène), requires a collar and leash year-round for dogs; category-1 dogs are banned and category-2 dogs must be muzzled. The park is reachable by car from Nice via the Route Métropolitaine de la Grande Corniche (RM 2465), heading towards La Turbie, as far as the Col d'Èze; the main car parks are at the Fort de la Revère and the Plateau de la Justice. The park is open from 7:30am to 8pm from April to October, and from 8am to 6pm from November to March. The Département specifies that some trail sections are closed to the public: follow the signs on site.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: head for the Fort de la Revère for a sweeping view over the entire bay of Villefranche, with a picnic area shaded by pines to rest after the walk.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The hilltop village of Èze, the Trophée d'Auguste in La Turbie and the bay of Villefranche-sur-Mer are just a few minutes away by car, to extend the outing.</p>
      <p>On the ground: the park's trails are waymarked, mostly on gravel, stones and packed earth — good terrain for paw pads, except in strong heat when exposed mineral surfaces can get hot. Bring your own water for your dog, especially in summer: the Département's page lists a "toilets / water point" among the park's facilities without saying where it is.</p>
      <p><strong>Additional rules:</strong> the park regulation bans animals from play areas, educational areas, fitness areas and sports trails. The Piste de la Forna is closed to the public until further notice (Département, updated 29/04/2026); the rest of the park remains open. The park has three discovery trails, picnic tables and an orientation table; camping and fires of any kind are banned.</p>
      <p><strong>Getting there:</strong> park address: route de la Revère, 06360 Èze. By bus, Lignes d'Azur 82 or 83, Col d'Èze stop, then a 25 to 40 minute walk to the Fort de la Revère. Mobile coverage is average to weak depending on the area.</p>
      <p><strong>Worth checking before you go:</strong> opening hours can be changed at any time for service or safety reasons (notice at the entrance), and so can the prefectural wildfire-risk order for the current year.</p>
      <p>Sources read on 06/11/2026: <a href="https://www.departement06.fr/annuaire-general/parc-de-la-grande-corniche">Alpes-Maritimes Département (park page)</a>, <a href="https://randoxygene.departement06.fr/sites/randoxygene/files/media/downloads/dpt06-parcs-departementaux_reglement-gdecorniche.pdf">park regulation</a>, <a href="https://explorateursdesparcs.departement06.fr/chapitre-2-parc-de-la-grande-corniche">Les Explorateurs des Alpes-Maritimes</a>.</p>
